P2b. the subtraction control, closed form against exhaustive sweep

  W       predicted        measured  verdict
  3       75.00000%       75.00000%  exact
  4       87.50000%       87.50000%  exact
  5       93.75000%       93.75000%  exact
  6       96.87500%       96.87500%  exact
  7       98.43750%       98.43750%  exact
  8       99.21875%       99.21875%  exact

largest gap over the swept widths: 0.000e+00

`94` section 4.2 reports 99.22%% at W = 8 for wrapping subtraction.
The closed form gives 1 - 2^-7 = 99.21875%, which is that number.

So the cell `94` cites as evidence that two permissions are independent is
a fact about subtraction in the integers. Wrapping contributes only the two
coincidences where 2c vanishes modulo the width. Nothing in it is about the
overflow policy, and nothing in it needs a permission bit.
